  <summary date="2026-11-20T15:28:53Z" status="Introduced in House">Afghanistan TPS Act of 2026

This bill grants Temporary Protected Status (TPS) to eligible nationals of Afghanistan. TPS makes protected individuals eligible for work authorization, prevents their detention on the basis of their immigration status, and precludes their removal from the United States.

To be eligible for&#160;TPS, an Afghan national must

remain continuously present in the United States after the date of enactment of this bill;&#160;be admissible as an immigrant;&#160;and&#160;register for&#160;TPS using established procedures, such as by submitting biometric and biographic data and completing criminal and national security background checks.In order to travel abroad, a&#160;TPS recipient under this bill must receive prior consent from the Department of Homeland Security by&#160;establishing that emergency and extenuating circumstances beyond the individual&#8217;s control require a brief, temporary trip abroad.

This designation begins on the date of enactment of this bill and ends on July 1, 2029.</summary>
